      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Pere Marquette Railroad reached Fostoria in 1881, turning the pine stand into a logging hub and later an agricultural shipping point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fostoria_michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By the early 1900s, Fostoria shifted from logging to farming once the white pine was exhausted.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fostoria_michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Fostoria Public Library houses a wide collection that reflects the town’s rich history.",
